# Go modules this project may depend on (direct or indirect). Adding one is an owner action:
# propose it, with a reason and the decision or standard that chose it. `make check` fails if
# go.mod names a module that is not listed here. Format: <module path>  # <reason> (<D-ID or standard>)

# Direct
modernc.org/sqlite  # pure-Go SQLite driver, no cgo; ncruces stays the benchmark alternative (D193, sql.md §7)
golang.org/x/crypto  # argon2id passwords and XChaCha20-Poly1305 sealed secrets (D194)
github.com/danielgtaylor/huma/v2  # the API and its generated OpenAPI on net/http (D193 §6)
github.com/BurntSushi/toml  # parses the config file and deploy/dev/seed.toml; no dependencies of its own (D197)
golang.org/x/text  # NFC filenames at the core's ingest (D49) and BCP 47 language tags from the probe (D206)
golang.org/x/image  # decodes and resizes the core's own sanitised WebP base images, the core's JPEG made from them; the Go team's (D212)
github.com/coder/websocket  # Watch Together's session WebSocket, the server side of cut-a §5.1; no dependencies of its own (D243 §10)
github.com/pion/logging  # pion/turn/v4's logger interface, through which the relay logs to slog (D243 §10)
github.com/pion/turn/v4  # the TURN relay embedded in the binary, which carries Watch Together's voice (D193 §4, D243 §8, §10)
github.com/pion/webrtc/v4  # WebRTC data channels, the direct path to a core behind carrier NAT whose client lacks IPv6; the owner, 2026-10-09: "Ok let's add webrtc" (D273 §7)

# Indirect: modernc.org/sqlite's closure
modernc.org/libc  # indirect, modernc.org/sqlite
modernc.org/mathutil  # indirect, modernc.org/sqlite
modernc.org/memory  # indirect, modernc.org/sqlite
github.com/dustin/go-humanize  # indirect, modernc.org/sqlite
github.com/google/uuid  # indirect, modernc.org/sqlite
github.com/mattn/go-isatty  # indirect, modernc.org/sqlite
github.com/ncruces/go-strftime  # indirect, modernc.org/sqlite
github.com/remyoudompheng/bigfft  # indirect, modernc.org/sqlite
golang.org/x/sys  # seccomp and Landlock for the node's confinement (D217 §4; cut-a §7); also indirect, modernc.org/sqlite and golang.org/x/crypto

# Indirect: github.com/pion/turn/v4's closure (D243 §10)
github.com/pion/dtls/v3  # indirect, github.com/pion/turn/v4
github.com/pion/randutil  # indirect, github.com/pion/turn/v4
github.com/pion/stun/v3  # indirect, github.com/pion/turn/v4; and the reachability check's STUN binding to the relay's port (D243 §7)
github.com/pion/transport/v3  # indirect, github.com/pion/turn/v4
github.com/pion/transport/v4  # indirect, github.com/pion/turn/v4
github.com/wlynxg/anet  # indirect, github.com/pion/turn/v4 (through pion/transport)

# Indirect: github.com/pion/webrtc/v4's closure (D273 §7)
github.com/pion/datachannel  # indirect, github.com/pion/webrtc/v4
github.com/pion/ice/v4  # indirect, github.com/pion/webrtc/v4
github.com/pion/interceptor  # indirect, github.com/pion/webrtc/v4
github.com/pion/mdns/v2  # indirect, github.com/pion/webrtc/v4
github.com/pion/rtcp  # indirect, github.com/pion/webrtc/v4
github.com/pion/rtp  # indirect, github.com/pion/webrtc/v4
github.com/pion/sctp  # indirect, github.com/pion/webrtc/v4
github.com/pion/sdp/v3  # indirect, github.com/pion/webrtc/v4
github.com/pion/srtp/v3  # indirect, github.com/pion/webrtc/v4
github.com/pion/stun/v4  # indirect, github.com/pion/webrtc/v4 (the relay's stun/v3 until it moves to turn/v5)
github.com/pion/transport/v5  # indirect, github.com/pion/webrtc/v4
github.com/pion/turn/v5  # indirect, github.com/pion/webrtc/v4 (the relay's turn/v4 until it moves to it)
golang.org/x/net  # indirect, github.com/pion/webrtc/v4; the Go team's
golang.org/x/time  # indirect, github.com/pion/webrtc/v4; the Go team's
